ed the amount paid.\\\",\\n  \\\"file\\\": \\\"app.py\\\",\\n  \\\"line\\\": 214,\\n  \\\"reviewed\\\": true\\n}\\n</untrusted>\\n\\n## Rules\\n<untrusted path=\\\"rules\\\">\\n[\\n  {\\n    \\\"broken_at_step\\\": 4,\\n    \\\"check\\\": \\\"order.refunded <= order.paid\\\",\\n    \\\"expected\\\": \\\"order.refunded <= order.paid\\\",\\n    \\\"id\\\": \\\"refund_le_paid\\\",\\n    \\\"kind\\\": \\\"state\\\",\\n    \\\"observed\\\": {\\n      \\\"paid\\\": 1,\\n      \\\"refunded\\\": 2,\\n      \\\"shipped\\\": false,\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"paid\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"reproduced\\\": \\\"10/10\\\",\\n    \\\"scope\\\": \\\"order\\\",\\n    \\\"text\\\": \\\"Total refunds never exceed the amount paid\\\"\\n  }\\n]\\n</untrusted>\\n\\n# Rules\\n- Reject a patch that does not address the diagnosed cause, weakens another rule, touches unrelated code,\\n  or edits tests to make them pass.\\n- List each issue as one short sentence; leave `issues` empty when you approve.\\n- The engine still verifies the fix by replay; you review the change only.\\n\\n# Output\\nExample of a valid final block (shape only; use the real data):\\n{\\\"issues\\\":[\\\"The fix also removes the stock check.\\\"],\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"reject\\\"}\\n\\nEnd your reply with exactly one ```json block matching this schema:\\n{\\\"additionalProperties\\\":false,\\\"properties\\\":{\\\"issues\\\":{\\\"items\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"string\\\"},\\\"title\\\":\\\"Issues\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"array\\\"},\\\"verdict\\\":{\\\"enum\\\":[\\\"approve\\\",\\\"reject\\\"],\\\"title\\\":\\\"Verdict\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"string\\\"}},\\\"required\\\":[\\\"verdict\\\"],\\\"title\\\":\\\"FixReviewOutput\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"object\\\"}\"}"}
